Professional Agent starter

Install rag-langgraph-lab into your Python environment first. No source-checkout
path or raglab service is needed. In this generated directory:

  python run.py
  python run.py --cases cases.jsonl
  python run.py --diagnose RUN_ID

Offline is a deterministic engineering fixture. It does not prove semantic model
quality, citation support, writing fidelity or general task completion.
For extraction/research only, explicitly opt into a paid model:

  Set OPENAI_API_KEY outside files, then:
  python run.py --mode openai --model YOUR_MODEL --cases cases.jsonl

The confirmed-action template uses a fixed workflow and needs no model. It saves
a local note only after exact approval. Inspect the displayed input/tool preview,
then provide the displayed run/review/digest explicitly:

  python run.py --resume RUN_ID --review-id REVIEW_ID --digest sha256:...

A business key reuses an identical note across Runs. Different content for the
same owner/key is rejected without changing the original note. Its bound receipt
stores JSON null as a durable not_applied fact; an absent receipt remains unknown.
Receipts are verified against owner, Agent, Run, binding, fingerprint and attempt.

The evaluator never approves. Expected awaiting_review cases are cancelled after
measurement and do not count as completed actions. Use a normal run to approve.

Edit agent.py for business schemas, instructions and tools. Extend cases.jsonl
with representative correct/incorrect/permission cases, then a held-out real-model
set. Source authorization and full domain quality require business implementation.
The research catalog is a tiny local fixture, not a production retrieval service.
SCOPES and the local identity are trusted single-user demonstration policies.
For a shared service, use create_agent_app with actual authentication and fresh
credential checks. Do not deploy this local identity resolver as public auth.

Runtime databases live in .runtime by default. Use a dedicated --data-dir. Preserve
matching Agent/component versions for recovery; request-key retries must reuse
identical input. Never commit .runtime, environment files or credentials.
Normal runs and exact approval resumes wait for the original Agent binding's
execution budget plus a one-second completion margin. Evaluation uses each case's
explicit timeout instead. An abnormal CLI exit closes its local runtime.
